## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical Dataflow streaming design with real-world concerns like per-tenant isolation and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub ingestion
- Dataflow streaming transforms and DoFn-like validation
- Per-tenant BigQuery datasets and environment isolation
- Idempotency/dedup and basic monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-Dataflow DoFn for validation
function validateEvent(record){
  if(!record.event_id || !record.tenant_id) throw new Error("Invalid");
  if(!record.event_ts) record.event_ts = Date.now();
  return record;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test idempotency under message replay?
- How would you cap cost for a high-volume tenant?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical ability to design basic multi-tenant isolation using GCP primitives, plus auth, observability, and testing without overengineering.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation via per-tenant resources
- JWT-derived tenant_id routing
- Single Cloud Run boundary with tenant-aware logic
- Per-tenant data storage (buckets/datasets) and strict IAM
- Observability (Cloud Logging/Monitoring) and simple test plan

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: extract tenant_id from JWT
function getTenantIdFromJwt(header){
  const token = header?.split(" ")[1];
  const payload = verifyAndDecode(token);
  return payload?.tenant_id;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce quotas per tenant without impacting others?
- What are trade-offs of per-tenant buckets vs. using per-tenant prefixes within a shared bucket?

